Two follow-ups from the 2026-04-28 production deploy:

1. src/server.ts outer catch — log error.name/message/stack as
   structured JSON before responding 500. Previously silent, which cost
   ~10 minutes diagnosing the volume-permission EACCES bug during deploy.
   Response shape unchanged for callers; only adds an ops-grep line.

2. apps/mail-api/deploy/ — first-class deploy bundle, version-controlled:
     - Dockerfile (node:22-alpine + su-exec entrypoint pattern)
     - docker-entrypoint.sh (chowns volume dir, drops to uid 1000)
     - bootstrap.mjs (createFlowApiServer + file-backed evidence sink)
     - README.md (build/ship/smoke/rollback procedure)

   The entrypoint self-heals the bind-mount-owned-by-root case that hit
   the 2026-04-28 deploy (host /var/lib/iai-mail-api was root:root,
   container ran as node uid 1000 → EACCES on first recordEvidence).
   Future deploys won't need a manual `chown 1000:1000` step.

Tests: 13/13 still passing (typecheck + build clean, integration tests
unchanged, server.ts logging is non-functional emission only).

Builds on commit 50d4a77 + deploy proof in
docs/iai-mail-platform/MAIL_IAI_ONE_INBOUND_WEBHOOK_PATH_B_DEPLOY_COMPLETE_2026-04-28.md

